 163:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c **** By default, after the Init and when the state is HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET
 164:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c **** all interrupt callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 165:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   examples HAL_TIM_TriggerCallback(), HAL_TIM_ErrorCallback().
 166:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 167:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 168:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are reset to the legacy weak
 169:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   functionalities in the Init / DeInit only when these callbacks are null
 170:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   (not registered beforehand). If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the Init / DeInit
 171:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit / MspDeInit callbacks(registered beforehand)
 172:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c **** 
 173:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   [..]
 174:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****     Callbacks can be registered / unregistered in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY state only.
 175:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****     Exception done MspInit / MspDeInit that can be registered / unregistered
 176:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****     in HAL_TIM_STATE_READY or HAL_TIM_STATE_RESET state,
 177:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****     thus registered(user) MspInit / DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init / DeInit.
 178:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 179:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_tim.c ****       using HAL_TIM_RegisterCallback() before calling DeInit or Init function.
